# Fulfilment and delivery operations analytics

**Business question:** where and why are we missing the delivery SLA and losing orders to defects, and what should operations change?

> **Simulated data.** Everything here comes from a seeded Python generator (`data_gen/generate.py`, seed {{ cfg.sim.seed }}), not from any real company. Assumptions: {{ cfg.sim.n_nodes }} fulfilment nodes in 5 zones, {{ cfg.sim.n_skus }} SKUs in 12 categories, about {{ (cfg.sim.target_orders / 1000) | int }}k orders over {{ cfg.sim.days }} days from {{ cfg.sim.start_date }}, Poisson demand with weekday/weekend hourly curves and rain uplift, pick and rider-wait times driven by queueing on rostered pickers and online riders, weather-dependent travel speed, daily order-up-to replenishment for the {{ cfg.sim.tracked_skus }} fastest SKUs, and refund claims for late, missing, wrong and damaged items. The delivery SLA is a config value ({{ cfg.ops.sla_minutes }} minutes here).

